+REPORT 02b — Status DONE
+
+Changes:
+- src/arci/demo/run.py
+  - New `failing_trial(run_dir)` used by step 3. It picks the candidate FAIL whose paired baseline is PASS with the smallest pair index (`int(pair_id.rsplit(":", 1)[1])`), not the first row in completion order. When no such pair exists it returns None, and step 3 still fails with "no pair where A passes and B fails".
+  - Step 3: a failing `arci diff` now prints `indented(diffed.stdout or diffed.stderr)`, the same way step 4 does.
+  - Step 2: new `RECORDED_PASSES = {"agent_b": (192, 132), "agent_a": (192, 192)}` and `recorded_comparison(candidate, counts)`. Each experiment prints one line, either "  matches the recorded run (A 192/200, <cand> N/200)" or "  differs from the recorded run (recorded A 192/200, <cand> N/200)". If the run did not complete (no counts), the line says it differs. `frozen_experiment` now returns True only when both experiments match. A difference never fails the step; the two verdict `expect`s still decide that.
+  - The final line comes from the new `final_line(work, matched=...)`: "Run stores: <dir>. Every count above was computed fresh on this machine, not replayed from evidence; they matched the recorded run (A 192/200, B 132/200)." or "...; they did not all match the recorded run (see step 2)."
+  - The trials.jsonl reader moved into a shared `_trials()`, used by `_candidate_passes` and `failing_trial`.
+- src/arci/cli.py (demo region only): the `--keep` help now reads "write the run stores to DIR (empty or new) instead of a kept temporary directory".
+- tests/unit/demo/test_demo.py: 13 new test cases (26 in total).
+  - (a) `test_the_last_line_names_the_store_and_the_recorded_comparison` [matched True/False]: monkeypatches all seven step functions and asserts the exact last two lines of `run_demo`, including `keep.resolve()`.
+  - (b) `_candidate_passes` is checked on the real noisy store in the existing step-logic test (it must agree with the row counts, and 0 <= B < A <= 12), plus `test_candidate_passes_counts_each_arm` on synthetic rows.
+  - (c) `test_failing_trial_is_the_smallest_pair_index_in_any_row_order` (5 shuffle seeds; the rows include decoys where the baseline fails or the candidate errors) and `test_failing_trial_is_none_without_an_a_pass_b_fail_pair`.
+  - Also `test_step_two_compares_with_the_recorded_run`, 4 cases covering the matching and differing lines and the no-counts case.
+
+Tests (run from the worktree):
+- .venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/demo -q -o addopts="" -> 26 passed in 2.68s
+- .venv/bin/ruff format --check . -> 230 files already formatted
+- .venv/bin/ruff check . -> All checks passed!
+- .venv/bin/basedpyright -> 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 notes
+- shasum -a 256 -c FROZEN.sha256 | grep -v OK -> no output
+- .venv/bin/python -m arci.cli demo --workers 8, run twice from an empty scratch directory: both exit 0 with empty stderr and nothing written to the current directory. The output of steps 3 and 4 is byte-identical between the two runs. Step 3 picked reserve-timeout:00005:candidate in both runs (read with `failing_trial` from each kept store). A separate 1-worker run of step 3 picked the same trial.
+  - Step 2 lines, run 1:
+      VERDICT: BLOCK (exit 1)   [A vs agent_b]
+      passed under the fault: A 192/200, agent_b 132/200
+      matches the recorded run (A 192/200, agent_b 132/200)
+      VERDICT: PASS (exit 0)   [A vs agent_a]
+      passed under the fault: A 192/200, agent_a 192/200
+      matches the recorded run (A 192/200, agent_a 192/200)
+  - Final line, run 1:
+      Run stores: /var/folders/.../T/arci-demo-1bxpi_k8. Every count above was computed fresh on this machine, not replayed from evidence; they matched the recorded run (A 192/200, B 132/200).
+
+Deviations:
+- The tests reach `_candidate_passes` through two `# pyright: ignore[reportPrivateUsage]` comments. The brief names that private helper, and renaming it would widen the public surface for test use only.
+- The step-3 output does not print the trial id, so the identical-id check was made by reading each kept store, not from stdout.
+
+Open issues:
+- Seen only while checking by hand, and outside my files: importing `arci.cli` for the first time while `sys.stdout` is redirected to a StringIO raises AttributeError, because `arci/mcp_boundary.py:70` reads `sys.stdout.buffer` at import. The demo itself is not affected: `arci()` imports `arci.cli` before it redirects, and the entry points import it at startup. It would only hit someone who calls `run_demo()` from library code while stdout is already redirected.
